== About me
I am a PhD candidate in the Electrical and Computer Engineering Department at UT Austin, where I am fortunate to be advised by [https://sites.google.com/view/sanjay-shakkottai/home Sanjay Shakkottai]. During my time at UT, I have also enjoyed collaborating with [https://sites.google.com/a/illinois.edu/srikant/ R. Srikant], [https://people.maths.bris.ac.uk/~maajg/ Ayalvadi Ganesh], [https://abishek90.github.io/ Abishek Sankararaman] and [https://sites.google.com/view/danielvial/ Daniel Vial].  

My research interests lie broadly in the fields of machine learning, optimization and networks. In particular, I am interested in developing efficient and reliable machine learning tools for real-life applications, and characterizing their theoretical and empirical behavior. My PhD thesis has focused on designing and analyzing communication-efficient decentralized algorithms in various multi-agent bandit settings. During my undergraduate degree, I worked on performance analysis of wireless networks.
	
